 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "**Test 3, Question 3 · Conditional distributions for continuous random variables** (10 marks)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "d5fe7133-a5c5-55e9-9ee4-bbeea0ef7812"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Same idea as Question 2, but with a formula $f_{X,Y}$. \"Given $Y=y$\" = stand on the horizontal line at height $y$. The conditional PDF is the joint PDF along that line, rescaled to have area $1$.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "1110bddd-4e29-54e0-b6a5-63430e11a90b"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "tone": "tip",
   "text": "**Formula sheet lines for this question** (it chains all of them):\n\n$$\nf_Y(y)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}f_{X,Y}(x,y)\\,dx\\quad\\longrightarrow\\quad f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{f_{X,Y}(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}\n$$\n\n$$\nF_X(x)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{x}f_X(t)\\,dt\\qquad\\text{(use it with }f_{X|Y}\\text{ for the conditional CDF)}\n$$\n\n$$\nE[X\\mid Y=y]=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}x\\,f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)\\,dx\n$$\n\nExpect the Lecture 21–22 chain: **$f_Y$ → $f_{X|Y}$ → $F_{X|Y}$ → a probability → $E[X\\mid Y=y]$ → independent?**",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "01c7d584-2784-5bb1-a437-c3f2e7a81901"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part A · Conditional PDF",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "bc57d325-5d60-5d2e-9853-7ed396e63ba7"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{f_{X,Y}(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}\\qquad\\text{for }y\\text{ with }f_Y(y)>0",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "27599022-bac4-4243-9a5e-0b4df18e3642"
    }
   ],
   "id": "e2e3aad3-367e-5b36-a5c8-8eb07b0dcfe2"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "**Slice:** fix $y$. Read the $x$ range off the inequalities (it may contain $y$).",
    "**Marginal:** integrate $f_{X,Y}$ over that $x$ range to get $f_Y(y)$.",
    "**Divide**, and write the range: \"for $0<x<y$, and $0$ otherwise; valid for $0<y<1$\"."
   ],
   "ordered": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "17ca15b3-fac7-526a-84b2-f7eaa89463f7"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Given $X=x$ instead? Swap the roles: vertical slice, $f_X(x)$, divide by $f_X(x)$.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "e56b02e2-be08-572a-a503-1f0c3fa1a587"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Move $y$. Where does the slice start and stop?\n\n```graph\ntitle \"Horizontal slice through $0<x<y<1$\"\nx -0.1 1.15 label=\"$x$\"\ny -0.1 1.15 label=\"$y$\"\nequal\nregion \"(x>0)*(y>x)*(y<1)\" color=1 label=\"where $f_{X,Y}\\ne0$\"\nslider s 0.05 0.95 0.5 label=\"$y$\"\ncurve \"x\" from=0 to=1 color=0 dash label=\"$y=x$\"\nsegment \"0\" \"s\" \"s\" \"s\" color=2 label=\"slice at $Y=y$: $x$ from $0$ to $y$\"\n```",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "dfc18f41-24d4-5cb6-9a56-7ad0bdf24d00"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 1 · A flat triangle ★ (Lectures 21–22)",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=2$ for $0<x<y<1$, and $0$ otherwise. Find $f_Y(y)$ and $f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Slice** at $y$: $x$ from $0$ to $y$.",
     "latex": ""
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Marginal.**",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\int_0^y2\\,dx=2y,\\qquad0<y<1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Divide.**",
     "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{2}{2y}=\\frac1y,\\qquad0<x<y\\quad(0<y<1)"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$f_Y=2y$ on $(0,1)$; $f_{X|Y}=\\tfrac1y$ on $(0,y)$: uniform on the slice",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "04ad4230-3a3a-4cca-9e73-930724b05690"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "e4d8b7bf-4c0d-4d5d-91de-e7c3678c21fc",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "8145df45-df73-4814-9233-49e2bb7dcc5c"
    }
   ],
   "id": "51787c06-7035-55c6-849b-53bb0ab7688b"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Flat $f$ → the conditional is uniform: height $=1/(\\text{slice length})$.",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "fb3c307e-9e19-53e5-be08-67671266718d"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 2 · A formula that is not flat ★ (Tutorial 7 Q5)",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=x+y$ for $0<x<1,\\ 0<y<1$. Find $f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Slice** at $y$: $x$ from $0$ to $1$. **Marginal.**",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\int_0^1(x+y)\\,dx=\\frac12+y"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Divide.**",
     "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{x+y}{y+\\frac12},\\qquad0<x<1\\quad(0<y<1)"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\dfrac{x+y}{y+1/2}$ on $(0,1)$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0fbffb43-2956-498c-9f5d-b1a897b31fdd"
    }
   ],
   "id": "e539a3b6-1881-5763-890e-581fcbfe4af2"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 1 · Vertical slice, curved region",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "**(a)** Same triangle $f=2$ on $0<x<y<1$: find $f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)$.\n\n**(b)** $f=\\tfrac{5y}{4}$ on $-1\\le x\\le1,\\ x^2\\le y\\le1$, with $f_Y=\\tfrac52y^{3/2}$: find $f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$. ★ Lecture 18",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Vertical slice:** $y$ from $x$ to $1$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}f_X(x)=\\int_x^12\\,dy=2(1-x) \\\\ f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)=\\frac{1}{1-x},\\qquad x<y<1\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Horizontal slice:** $-\\sqrt y\\le x\\le\\sqrt y$. **Divide.**",
     "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{5y/4}{\\frac52y^{3/2}}=\\frac1{2\\sqrt y},\\qquad|x|\\le\\sqrt y"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\tfrac1{1-x}$ on $(x,1)$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac1{2\\sqrt y}$ on $[-\\sqrt y,\\sqrt y]$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "0f47f931-b362-40d3-8be9-68ad8c24477a",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "2e2d07ef-0fa1-4599-92c9-e91fa179e9d1"
    }
   ],
   "id": "422c2fc0-0725-525f-848a-3b28377aa60a"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part B · Conditional CDF and probabilities",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "58aef1c9-9097-50f2-992f-bbbaab5f9aae"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "F_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=P(X\\le x\\mid Y=y)=\\int_{-\\infty}^{x}f_{X|Y}(u\\mid y)\\,du",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "13df79ff-e9d2-4459-a1c6-4c61d0825c20",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "27599022-bac4-4243-9a5e-0b4df18e3642"
    }
   ],
   "id": "d1a32354-a499-54d2-9d2f-9612741f3ba5"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "Three pieces: **$0$** before the slice, **$\\int$ from the slice start to $x$** inside, **$1$** after.",
    "For a probability, put the number $y$ in first. Then $P(a<X<b\\mid Y=y)=\\int_a^b f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)\\,dx$, using only the part inside the slice.",
    "Continuous: $<$ and $\\le$ give the same answer."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "662decfd-3433-51c1-bb23-85b593bd5221"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 3 · Triangle CDF ★ (Lecture 22)",
   "prompt": "With $f_{X|Y}=\\tfrac1y$ on $0<x<y$ (Part A), find $F_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$ and $P(X<\\tfrac14\\mid Y=\\tfrac12)$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Inside** ($0<x<y$).",
     "latex": "\\int_0^x\\frac1y\\,du=\\frac xy"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**All three pieces.**",
     "latex": "F_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\begin{cases}0,&x\\le0\\\\ \\dfrac xy,&0<x<y\\\\ 1,&x\\ge y\\end{cases}\\qquad(0<y<1)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Plug in** $x=\\tfrac14,\\ y=\\tfrac12$.",
     "latex": "P\\big(X<\\frac14\\ \\big|\\ Y=\\frac12\\big)=\\frac{1/4}{1/2}=\\frac12"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$0$, $\\tfrac xy$, $1$; $\\tfrac12$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "e4d8b7bf-4c0d-4d5d-91de-e7c3678c21fc",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "ae15266d-60e3-4ebc-9b77-fd6d6fdf89b5"
    }
   ],
   "id": "8e225fc4-487d-515a-abaa-d74ad9e649b2"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 2 · Not flat ★ (Tutorial 7 Q5 PDF)",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\dfrac{x+y}{y+\\frac12}$ on $0<x<1$ (Part A). Find $F_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$ and $P(X<\\tfrac12\\mid Y=\\tfrac12)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Inside.**",
     "latex": "F_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\int_0^x\\frac{u+y}{y+\\frac12}\\,du=\\frac{\\frac{x^2}{2}+xy}{y+\\frac12},\\qquad0<x<1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "$0$ for $x\\le0$, $1$ for $x\\ge1$. **Plug in** $y=\\tfrac12$ (bottom $=1$), $x=\\tfrac12$.",
     "latex": "\\frac18+\\frac14=\\frac38"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\dfrac{x^2/2+xy}{y+1/2}$ on $(0,1)$; $\\tfrac38$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0fbffb43-2956-498c-9f5d-b1a897b31fdd"
    }
   ],
   "id": "05d55259-8061-59ba-a0cc-acdc37164d92"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 1,
   "text": "Part C · Conditional expectation",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "a869b7f3-858f-5383-abaa-dc83d604d9d6"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "C1 · $E[X\\mid Y=y]$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9d23896f-c4e6-5c97-9fb2-1f52c3fb0ca0"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}x\\,f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)\\,dx",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "e4d8b7bf-4c0d-4d5d-91de-e7c3678c21fc",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "5ad2282c-1474-44fa-ad34-94fab76cd986"
    }
   ],
   "id": "69a0164f-bb9f-54f0-b12c-1c868eea6f96"
  },
  {
   "type": "list",
   "items": [
    "Integrate over the slice only. The answer is usually a formula in $y$.",
    "**Shortcut:** uniform on $(a,b)$ → mean $=\\tfrac{a+b}2$. Triangle: $E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\tfrac y2$.",
    "Independent → $E[X\\mid Y=y]=E[X]$, a fixed number. If it **changes with $y$**, they are dependent, even on a rectangle."
   ],
   "ordered": false,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "6b9f85f9-228e-5b00-843d-28e11488b801"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 4 · Mean, then independence ★ (Lecture 22)",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=6xy(2-x-y)$ for $0<x<1,\\ 0<y<1$.\n\n**(a)** Find $E[X\\mid Y=y]$.\n\n**(b)** Are $X$ and $Y$ independent?",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Marginal.**",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\int_0^1 6xy(2-x-y)\\,dx=6y\\Big(1-\\frac13-\\frac y2\\Big)=y(4-3y)"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Divide.**",
     "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{6x(2-x-y)}{4-3y},\\qquad0<x<1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Mean.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\frac{6}{4-3y}\\int_0^1x^2(2-x-y)\\,dx \\\\ =\\frac{6}{4-3y}\\Big(\\frac23-\\frac14-\\frac y3\\Big) \\\\ =\\frac{5-4y}{2(4-3y)},\\qquad0<y<1\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) It **changes with $y$** (e.g. $\\tfrac58$ near $y=0$, $\\tfrac12$ near $y=1$) → **dependent**, even though the region is a square.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\dfrac{5-4y}{2(4-3y)}$\n\n**(b)** dependent",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "e4d8b7bf-4c0d-4d5d-91de-e7c3678c21fc",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "e45fceff-56ef-4197-8f13-d60d0a09adb2"
    }
   ],
   "id": "c3d9c1bc-0b34-58bb-ad54-e15a1edaf881"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 3 · Two quick means",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "**(a)** $f=x+y$ on the unit square. Find $E[X\\mid Y=y]$.\n\n**(b)** $f=e^{-y}$ for $0<x<y$. Find $f_{X|Y}$ and $E[X\\mid Y=y]$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Weight** $\\tfrac{x+y}{y+1/2}$ (Part A).",
     "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\frac{\\int_0^1x(x+y)\\,dx}{y+\\frac12}=\\frac{\\frac13+\\frac y2}{y+\\frac12}=\\frac{2+3y}{3(1+2y)}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Slice** $0<x<y$: $f_Y=ye^{-y}$, so $f_{X|Y}=\\tfrac1y$. Uniform → midpoint.",
     "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\frac y2"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\dfrac{2+3y}{3(1+2y)}$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac1y$ on $(0,y)$; $\\tfrac y2$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0fbffb43-2956-498c-9f5d-b1a897b31fdd"
    }
   ],
   "id": "33353129-7426-50c4-905c-bf4743dd17d4"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "C2 · $E[g(X)\\mid Y=y]$ (Lecture 23)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "e114ba17-254a-530b-a222-0c2b09bbc6a6"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Put $g(x)$ in front instead of $x$. For the variance use $g(x)=x^2$, then subtract the mean squared.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "625ace99-ee24-45d3-afdd-300316ee5b2b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "a1812630-fc1b-4785-ab54-9ae927229b54"
    }
