  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 5 · $E[g(X)\\mid Y=1]$ ★ (Lecture 23)",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=\\tfrac12\\,y\\,e^{-xy}$ for $0<x<\\infty,\\ 0<y<2$. Find $E[e^{X/2}\\mid Y=1]$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Marginal:** slice $x$ from $0$ to $\\infty$.",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\int_0^\\infty\\frac12ye^{-xy}\\,dx=\\frac12,\\qquad0<y<2"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Divide**, then put $y=1$.",
     "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=ye^{-xy}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad f_{X|Y}(x\\mid1)=e^{-x},\\ x>0"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Put $g(x)=e^{x/2}$ in front.**",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}E[e^{X/2}\\mid Y=1]=\\int_0^\\infty e^{x/2}e^{-x}\\,dx=\\int_0^\\infty e^{-x/2}\\,dx \\\\ =\\Big[-2e^{-x/2}\\Big]_0^\\infty=2\\end{gathered}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$2$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "625ace99-ee24-45d3-afdd-300316ee5b2b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "c9932488-fdb1-4981-b219-d7325f2e9c1a"
    },
    {
     "source_id": "625ace99-ee24-45d3-afdd-300316ee5b2b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "4ac5f29a-03a0-48e6-b5ad-479b25d5491f"
    }
   ],
   "id": "43ae1cba-6f6e-54ac-9053-baaf9967989c"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 4 · Conditional variance",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$f=e^{-y}$ for $0<x<y$, so $f_{X|Y}=\\tfrac1y$ on $(0,y)$. Find $\\operatorname{Var}(X\\mid Y=y)$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Square.**",
     "latex": "E[X^2\\mid Y=y]=\\int_0^y\\frac{x^2}{y}\\,dx=\\frac{y^2}{3}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Subtract** the mean squared ($\\tfrac y2$).",
     "latex": "\\frac{y^2}3-\\frac{y^2}4=\\frac{y^2}{12}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac{y^2}{12}$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "b4c6d81a-5a8a-537b-a8ce-97846c8cbb74"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "C3 · Total expectation (Lecture 23)",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "a42b17c5-92ff-54e4-9e82-db117ded95dc"
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "text": "Same rule as Question 2, with an integral: weight $E[X\\mid Y=y]$ by $f_Y(y)$.",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "625ace99-ee24-45d3-afdd-300316ee5b2b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "35191376-1a9a-45fd-9a70-2d6c5a690139"
    }
   ],
   "id": "3927888f-e8f1-5888-a86c-9989c20be004"
  },
  {
   "type": "equation",
   "latex": "E[X]=\\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty}E[X\\mid Y=y]\\,f_Y(y)\\,dy",
   "display": true,
   "citations": [],
   "id": "36ae570e-7e12-5336-abb1-b167df95fc17"
  },
  {
   "type": "worked_example",
   "title": "Example 6 · Back to the triangle",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}=2$ on $0<x<y<1$. Use $E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\tfrac y2$ (C1) and $f_Y=2y$ (Part A) to find $E[X]$.",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Weight and integrate.**",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\int_0^1\\frac y2\\cdot2y\\,dy=\\int_0^1y^2\\,dy=\\frac13"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "**Check** with $f_X=2(1-x)$ (Part A Try it).",
     "latex": "\\int_0^1x\\cdot2(1-x)\\,dx=1-\\frac23=\\frac13\\ \\checkmark"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$\\tfrac13$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "9d2d08d7-62f5-514c-90f8-fcc1ae5beed4"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Try it 5 · Your turn",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$f=e^{-y}$ for $0<x<y$. You know $E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\tfrac y2$ and $f_Y=ye^{-y}$ for $y>0$. Find $E[X]$.",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "**Weight and integrate.** Use $\\int_0^\\infty y^2e^{-y}\\,dy=2$.",
     "latex": "E[X]=\\int_0^\\infty\\frac y2\\cdot ye^{-y}\\,dy=\\frac12\\cdot2=1"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "$1$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "24efb3c8-d034-552d-908c-9bac9b8f2bca"
  },
