  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 1 · [10 marks] The mirror triangle ★ (Tutorial 8 Q2 PDF)",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=2$ for $0\\le y\\le x\\le1$, and $0$ otherwise.\n\n**(a)** Find $f_X(x)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $F_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Find $P(Y<\\tfrac14\\mid X=\\tfrac12)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(e)** Find $E[Y\\mid X=x]$. Are $X,Y$ independent? (2 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Vertical slice:** $y$ from $0$ to $x$.",
     "latex": "f_X(x)=\\int_0^x2\\,dy=2x,\\qquad0<x\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Divide.**",
     "latex": "f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)=\\frac{2}{2x}=\\frac1x,\\qquad0\\le y\\le x"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Three pieces.**",
     "latex": "F_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)=\\begin{cases}0,&y<0\\\\ \\dfrac yx,&0\\le y\\le x\\\\ 1,&y>x\\end{cases}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **Plug in.**",
     "latex": "F_{Y|X}\\big(\\frac14\\mid\\frac12\\big)=\\frac{1/4}{1/2}=\\frac12"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(e) **Uniform on $(0,x)$** → midpoint. It changes with $x$ → **dependent**.",
     "latex": "E[Y\\mid X=x]=\\frac x2"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $2x$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac1x$ on $[0,x]$\n\n**(c)** $0,\\ \\tfrac yx,\\ 1$\n\n**(d)** $\\tfrac12$\n\n**(e)** $\\tfrac x2$; dependent",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "7d80bdef-0a85-4aa8-8247-f4431ad8aec6",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "07a91314-e9cd-45cd-b397-35b10dd7bfd3"
    }
   ],
   "id": "eaa867bd-0ffe-5322-9579-38dd24dab4cb"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 2 · [10 marks] A triangle with $24xy$ ★ (Tutorial 7 Q6 PDF)",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=24xy$ for $x\\ge0,\\ y\\ge0,\\ x+y\\le1$.\n\n**(a)** Find $f_Y(y)$. (3 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $P(X<\\tfrac14\\mid Y=\\tfrac12)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Find $E[X\\mid Y=y]$. (3 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Horizontal slice:** $x$ from $0$ to $1-y$.",
     "latex": "f_Y(y)=\\int_0^{1-y}24xy\\,dx=12y(1-y)^2,\\qquad0\\le y\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Divide.**",
     "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{24xy}{12y(1-y)^2}=\\frac{2x}{(1-y)^2},\\qquad0\\le x\\le1-y"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Put $y=\\tfrac12$:** $f=8x$ on $(0,\\tfrac12)$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^{1/4}8x\\,dx=4\\cdot\\frac1{16}=\\frac14"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\int_0^{1-y}\\frac{2x^2}{(1-y)^2}\\,dx=\\frac{2(1-y)^3}{3(1-y)^2}=\\frac{2(1-y)}{3}"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $12y(1-y)^2$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac{2x}{(1-y)^2}$ on $[0,1-y]$\n\n**(c)** $\\tfrac14$\n\n**(d)** $\\tfrac23(1-y)$",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "79f52518-90e0-41df-b0b0-5800904bbe9b",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "0fbffb43-2956-498c-9f5d-b1a897b31fdd"
    }
   ],
   "id": "872e0ad9-9680-54e3-905f-2b37be6c26fb"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 3 · [10 marks] Given $X$ on a square ★ (Tutorial 8 Q8 PDF)",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "source",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=x+y$ for $0\\le x\\le1,\\ 0\\le y\\le1$.\n\n**(a)** Find $f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)$. (3 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $P(Y>\\tfrac12\\mid X=0)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $E[Y\\mid X=x]$. (3 marks)\n\n**(d)** Use (c) to decide if $X,Y$ are independent. (2 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Marginal** $f_X=x+\\tfrac12$. **Divide.**",
     "latex": "f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)=\\frac{x+y}{x+\\frac12},\\qquad0\\le y\\le1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Put $x=0$:** $f=2y$.",
     "latex": "\\int_{1/2}^1 2y\\,dy=1-\\frac14=\\frac34"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Mean.**",
     "latex": "E[Y\\mid X=x]=\\frac{\\int_0^1y(x+y)\\,dy}{x+\\frac12}=\\frac{\\frac x2+\\frac13}{x+\\frac12}=\\frac{3x+2}{3(2x+1)}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) At $x=0$ it is $\\tfrac23$, at $x=1$ it is $\\tfrac59$. It changes → **dependent**.",
     "latex": ""
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\tfrac{x+y}{x+1/2}$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac34$\n\n**(c)** $\\tfrac{3x+2}{3(2x+1)}$\n\n**(d)** dependent",
   "citations": [
    {
     "source_id": "7d80bdef-0a85-4aa8-8247-f4431ad8aec6",
     "version": 1,
     "chunk_id": "3ab01077-9980-4b23-ba3e-e7135c520c63"
    }
   ],
   "id": "772efd07-2bb7-5f6a-8551-9c7edaf0fc42"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 4 · [10 marks] An exponential pair",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=e^{-y}$ for $0<x<y$, and $0$ otherwise.\n\n**(a)** Find $f_X(x)$ and $f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)$. (4 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $P(Y>x+1\\mid X=x)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $E[Y\\mid X=x]$. (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Find $f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$. (2 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Vertical slice:** $y$ from $x$ to $\\infty$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}f_X(x)=\\int_x^\\infty e^{-y}\\,dy=e^{-x},\\qquad x>0 \\\\ f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)=\\frac{e^{-y}}{e^{-x}}=e^{-(y-x)},\\qquad y>x\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Integrate** from $x+1$.",
     "latex": "\\int_{x+1}^\\infty e^{-(y-x)}\\,dy=e^{-1}\\approx0.368"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Mean** (substitute $t=y-x$).",
     "latex": "E[Y\\mid X=x]=\\int_x^\\infty y\\,e^{-(y-x)}\\,dy=x+1"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **Horizontal slice** $0<x<y$: $f_Y=ye^{-y}$.",
     "latex": "f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{e^{-y}}{ye^{-y}}=\\frac1y,\\qquad0<x<y"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $e^{-x}$; $e^{-(y-x)}$ on $y>x$\n\n**(b)** $e^{-1}$\n\n**(c)** $x+1$\n\n**(d)** $\\tfrac1y$ on $(0,y)$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "d3a0bebe-cd2e-5cb2-9e29-4b1caf285342"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 5 · [10 marks] Like Lecture 23",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=\\tfrac12\\,y\\,e^{-xy}$ for $x>0,\\ 0<y<2$.\n\n**(a)** Find $f_Y(y)$ and $f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$. (3 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $P(X>1\\mid Y=2)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $E[X\\mid Y=y]$. (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Find $E[e^{X}\\mid Y=2]$. (3 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Slice** $x$ from $0$ to $\\infty$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}f_Y(y)=\\frac12,\\quad0<y<2 \\\\ f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=ye^{-xy},\\quad x>0\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Put $y=2$:** $f=2e^{-2x}$.",
     "latex": "\\int_1^\\infty2e^{-2x}\\,dx=e^{-2}\\approx0.135"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Mean** (exponential with rate $y$).",
     "latex": "E[X\\mid Y=y]=\\int_0^\\infty x\\,ye^{-xy}\\,dx=\\frac1y"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) **$g(x)=e^x$**, $y=2$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^\\infty e^{x}\\cdot2e^{-2x}\\,dx=2\\int_0^\\infty e^{-x}\\,dx=2"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $\\tfrac12$; $ye^{-xy}$\n\n**(b)** $e^{-2}$\n\n**(c)** $\\tfrac1y$\n\n**(d)** $2$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "2444fce8-36ba-5193-9c33-b655fcea3378"
  },
  {
   "type": "practice_problem",
   "title": "Question 6 · [10 marks] Find $c$ first",
   "difficulty": "intermediate",
   "origin": "original",
   "prompt": "$f_{X,Y}(x,y)=c\\,x$ for $0<y<x<1$, and $0$ otherwise.\n\n**(a)** Find $c$. (2 marks)\n\n**(b)** Find $f_Y(y)$ and $f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)$. (4 marks)\n\n**(c)** Find $P(X>\\tfrac12\\mid Y=0.2)$. (2 marks)\n\n**(d)** Find $f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)$ and $E[Y\\mid X=x]$. (2 marks)",
   "solution": "",
   "steps": [
    {
     "explanation": "(a) **Slice** $y$ from $0$ to $x$.",
     "latex": "\\int_0^1\\!\\!\\int_0^x cx\\,dy\\,dx=c\\int_0^1x^2\\,dx=\\frac c3=1\\ \\Rightarrow\\ c=3"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(b) **Horizontal slice:** $x$ from $y$ to $1$.",
     "latex": "\\begin{gathered}f_Y(y)=\\int_y^13x\\,dx=\\frac32(1-y^2),\\qquad0<y<1 \\\\ f_{X|Y}(x\\mid y)=\\frac{3x}{\\frac32(1-y^2)}=\\frac{2x}{1-y^2},\\qquad y<x<1\\end{gathered}"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(c) **Put $y=0.2$:** $1-y^2=0.96$.",
     "latex": "\\int_{0.5}^1\\frac{2x}{0.96}\\,dx=\\frac{1-0.25}{0.96}=\\frac{0.75}{0.96}=0.78125"
    },
    {
     "explanation": "(d) $f_X=3x^2$. **Divide:** flat in $y$ → uniform on $(0,x)$.",
     "latex": "f_{Y|X}(y\\mid x)=\\frac{3x}{3x^2}=\\frac1x,\\quad0<y<x;\\qquad E[Y\\mid X=x]=\\frac x2"
    }
   ],
   "answer": "**(a)** $3$\n\n**(b)** $\\tfrac32(1-y^2)$; $\\tfrac{2x}{1-y^2}$ on $(y,1)$\n\n**(c)** $0.78125=\\tfrac{25}{32}$\n\n**(d)** $\\tfrac1x$; $\\tfrac x2$",
   "citations": [],
   "id": "557ab328-b764-5745-8a3b-fb7a942cc13c"
  },
